{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CZQaeYTggw5kTUGuCHbVY3","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t# CONFIGS.md — Phase A.3: configuration-surface table\n     2\t\n     3\t## Mechanical derivation of the axes\n     4\t\n     5\t### Public entry points (complete set)\n     6\t\n     7\t`nm -D` on the C `.so` exports exactly one function, and the header declares\n     8\texactly one function:\n     9\t\n    10\t| entry point | signature | is it a convenience wrapper? |\n    11\t|---|---|---|\n    12\t| `max_size_frame` | `tflac_u32 (tflac_u32 blocksize, tflac_u32 channels, tflac_u32 bitdepth)` | **No.** It is simultaneously the highest- and lowest-level entry point. It calls nothing (leaf function), has no `static` helpers, no init/teardown, and no hidden state. |\n    13\t\n    14\tThere is therefore no \"call hierarchy\" to walk and no lower-level API hiding\n    15\tbehind a one-shot wrapper — the single export *is* the low-level API. Confirmed\n    16\tby `SYMBOLS.md`'s completeness audit of the 15 total lines of C.\n    17\t\n    18\t### Build-time configuration axes\n    19\t\n    20\t* `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` table** ⇒ the only valid feature\n    21\t  combination is the empty set. Enumerated and verified by\n    22\t  `./check_all_features.sh` (1 combination, plus the `default` and\n    23\t  `--all-features` invocations, which are identical to it here).\n    24\t* `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` defines **no** `option()`, `add_definitions`,\n    25\t  `target_compile_definitions`, or conditional sources — it unconditionally\n    26\t  compiles `src/lib.c`. `grep -nE '#if'` over the C source has **no matches**,\n    27\t  so there is no `#ifdef`-selected code either.\n    28\t\n    29\t⇒ **One build configuration total.** All rows below are runtime-input rows.\n    30\t\n    31\t### Runtime axes the C code actually branches on\n    32\t\n    33\tDerived from the three predicates and the arithmetic in `src/lib.c:4-9`:\n    34\t\n    35\t```c\n    36\treturn 18U + channels +\n    37\t       (((blocksize * bitdepth * (channels * (channels != 2))) +   /* T1 */\n    38\t         (blocksize * bitdepth * (channels == 2)) +                /* T2 */\n    39\t         (blocksize * (bitdepth + (bitdepth != 32)) * (channels == 2)) + /* T3 */\n    40\t         +7) / 8);\n    41\t```\n    42\t\n    43\t| axis | values the code distinguishes | why (source evidence) |\n    44\t|---|---|---|\n    45\t| **X1 — stereo predicate** | `channels == 2` vs `channels != 2` | `(channels != 2)` gates `T1`; `(channels == 2)` gates `T2` and `T3`. The two branches are mutually exclusive, so they are genuinely different code paths. |\n    46\t| **X2 — zero-channel degeneracy** | `channels == 0` vs `channels > 0` | `channels * (channels != 2)` is `0` when `channels == 0`, zeroing `T1` even on the non-stereo path. |\n    47\t| **X3 — bit-depth predicate** | `bitdepth == 32` vs `bitdepth != 32` | `(bitdepth != 32)` adds `1` to `bitdepth` inside `T3`. Only observable when `channels == 2`, so X3 must be crossed with X1. |\n    48\t| **X4 — blocksize magnitude** | `0`, `1`, small, realistic, `65535`, `2^24`, `UINT32_MAX` | Multiplicand of all three terms; `0` zeroes the numerator, large values drive 32-bit wrap. |\n    49\t| **X5 — bitdepth magnitude** | `0`, `1..31`, `32`, `33..64`, huge, `UINT32_MAX` | `bitdepth == 0` makes `T3 == blocksize`; `UINT32_MAX` makes `bitdepth + 1` wrap to `0`. |\n    50\t| **X6 — 32-bit wrap of the products** | no wrap vs wrap | Unsigned `*` is mod 2^32; wrapping changes the numerator and hence the result. |\n    51\t| **X7 — ceiling-divide residue** | `numerator mod 8 ∈ {0,…,7}` | The `+7 ... / 8` idiom rounds up; each of the 8 residues is a distinct rounding outcome. |\n    52\t| **X8 — wrap of `numerator + 7`** | `sum + 7` fits vs overflows | When `sum` is within 7 of `UINT32_MAX` the `+7` wraps, so the divide sees a *tiny* numerator instead of a huge one. |\n    53\t| **X9 — wrap of the outer `18U + channels`** | fits vs overflows | `channels` near `UINT32_MAX` wraps the final sum. |\n    54\t\n    55\tAxes that are **N/A** for this library (recorded so the pruning is auditable):\n    56\telement type / width (every parameter and the return are `uint32_t`), byte order\n    57\tand format (nothing is serialized, no memory is read or written), counts and\n    58\t\"empty / one / many\" collections (there is no array, buffer, or length\n    59\tparameter), and runtime option/mode/flag state (there is no context struct,\n    60\tno setter, and no global).\n    61\t\n    62\t## Configuration-surface table\n    63\t\n    64\tEvery row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** drawn inside that row's\n    65\tconstraint (fixed seed `0x5EED_C0FFEE` + per-row salt, splitmix64 PRNG in\n    66\t`tests/common/mod.rs`), not one hand-picked value. Rows 22–24 are *exhaustive*\n    67\tover their stated domain. All rows live in `tests/differential.rs` and call both\n    68\t`.so` files through `libloading`.\n    69\t\n    70\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | axes | [ ] |\n    71\t|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|------|-----|\n    72\t| 1 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth == 32` (the equality-guarded value), `blocksize` random `1..=65535` | X1,X3 | [x] |\n    73\t| 2 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth == 16` (≠32), `blocksize` random `1..=65535` | X1,X3 | [x] |\n    74\t| 3 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth` random `1..=31`, `blocksize` random `1..=65535` | X1,X3,X5 | [x] |\n    75\t| 4 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth` random `33..=64`, `blocksize` random `1..=65535` | X1,X3,X5 | [x] |\n    76\t| 5 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth == 0`, `blocksize` random full 32-bit (`T3` collapses to `blocksize`) | X1,X5,X6 | [x] |\n    77\t| 6 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth == UINT32_MAX` (inner `+1` wraps to `0`), `blocksize` random full range | X1,X5,X6 | [x] |\n    78\t| 7 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 2`, `bitdepth` **and** `blocksize` random full 32-bit (stereo path with heavy wrapping) | X1,X5,X6,X8 | [x] |\n    79\t| 8 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 0`, `bitdepth`/`blocksize` random full range (all terms vanish) | X2 | [x] |\n    80\t| 9 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 1` (mono), `bitdepth ∈ {4,8,12,16,20,24,32}`, `blocksize` realistic FLAC sizes | X1,X2 | [x] |\n    81\t| 10 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == 3`, `bitdepth` random `1..=32`, `blocksize` random `1..=65535` (just past the stereo special case) | X1,X3 | [x] |\n    82\t| 11 | `max_size_frame` | `channels` random `4..=8`, `bitdepth ∈ {4,8,12,16,20,24,32}`, `blocksize` realistic | X1 | [x] |\n    83\t| 12 | `max_size_frame` | `channels` random `9..=255`, `bitdepth` random `1..=64`, `blocksize` random `1..=8192` | X1 | [x] |\n    84\t| 13 | `max_size_frame` | `channels` random `2^16..2^32` (≠2) with non-zero `blocksize`/`bitdepth` — forces `T1` wrap **and** outer wrap | X1,X6,X9 | [x] |\n    85\t| 14 | `max_size_frame` | `channels == UINT32_MAX`, `blocksize`/`bitdepth` random full range | X6,X9 | [x] |\n    86\t| 15 | `max_size_frame` | `blocksize == 0`, `channels`/`bitdepth` random full range (result must be `18 + channels`) | X4,X9 | [x] |\n    87\t| 16 | `max_size_frame` | `blocksize == 1`, `channels`/`bitdepth` random full range | X4,X6 | [x] |\n    88\t| 17 | `max_size_frame` | `blocksize == UINT32_MAX`, `channels` random `0..=8`, `bitdepth` random `0..=64` | X4,X6 | [x] |\n    89\t| 18 | `max_size_frame` | `blocksize` = every power of two `2^0..2^31`, crossed with `channels ∈ {1,2,3}` and `bitdepth ∈ {16,24,32}` (exhaustive) | X4,X6 | [x] |\n    90\t| 19 | `max_size_frame` | Non-stereo rounding sweep: `channels == 1`, `bitdepth == 1`, `blocksize` chosen to hit **every** residue `numerator mod 8 == 0..7` | X7 | [x] |\n    91\t| 20 | `max_size_frame` | Stereo rounding sweep: `channels == 2`, `bitdepth == 1` (`sum == 3*blocksize`), `blocksize` chosen to hit every residue | X1,X7 | [x] |\n    92\t| 21 | `max_size_frame` | Numerator engineered into `[UINT32_MAX-6, UINT32_MAX]` so `sum + 7` itself wraps | X8 | [x] |\n    93\t| 22 | `max_size_frame` | **Exhaustive** small cube: `blocksize 0..=48` × `channels 0..=8` × `bitdepth 0..=40` (18 081 calls) | X1,X2,X3,X4,X5,X7 | [x] |\n    94\t| 23 | `max_size_frame` | **Exhaustive** single-axis sweeps: `channels 0..=1024` at realistic `blocksize`/`bitdepth`; `bitdepth 0..=64`; `blocksize 0..=4096` | X1,X2,X3,X4,X5 | [x] |\n    95\t| 24 | `max_size_frame` | **Exhaustive** FLAC-realistic matrix: `blocksize ∈ {192,576,1152,2304,4608,256,512,1024,2048,4096,8192,16384,32768,65535}` × `channels 1..=8` × `bitdepth ∈ {4,8,12,16,20,24,32}` | X1,X3,X4,X5 | [x] |\n    96\t| 25 | `max_size_frame` | Uniform random full-range triples, 200 000 iterations (unconstrained fuzz) | all | [x] |\n    97\t| 26 | `max_size_frame` | Mixed boundary/random: each argument independently drawn from the boundary set `{0,1,2,3,4,7,8,31,32,33,64,4096,65535,65536,2^31-1,2^31,2^32-2,2^32-1}` ∪ uniform random — covers every boundary *interaction* | all | [x] |\n    98\t\n    99\t**Total rows: 26.** Each is checked off only after passing across all of its\n   100\trandomized inputs.\n   101\t\n   102\t## Feature-combination coverage\n   103\t\n   104\tBecause there is exactly one valid feature combination (no `[features]` table),\n   105\trunning the suite once covers \"every feature combination\". `run_all_tests.sh`\n   106\tnevertheless drives the full suite through `--no-default-features`, `default`,\n   107\tand `--all-features` so the claim is machine-checked rather than argued.\n########## SYMBOLS.md\n     1\t# SYMBOLS.md — Phase A.1: exported-symbol parity\n     2\t\n     3\tMechanically derived from `nm -D` on both shared libraries. Nothing here is\n     4\tassumed; every row is copied from the tool output reproduced below.\n     5\t\n     6\t## Build commands\n     7\t\n     8\t```sh\n     9\t# C shared library\n    10\tcd translated_rust/c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build\n    11\tcmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .\n    12\t#   -> c_src/build/libtranslated_rust.so\n    13\t\n    14\t# Rust shared library (crate-type = [\"cdylib\"], lib name = max_size_frame_lib)\n    15\tcd translated_rust && cargo build\n    16\t#   -> target/debug/libmax_size_frame_lib.so\n    17\t```\n    18\t\n    19\t## Raw `nm -D --defined-only` output\n    20\t\n    21\tC library (`c_src/build/libtranslated_rust.so`):\n    22\t\n    23\t```\n    24\t00000000000010f9 T max_size_frame\n    25\t```\n    26\t\n    27\tRust library (`target/debug/libmax_size_frame_lib.so`):\n    28\t\n    29\t```\n    30\t0000000000011dc0 T max_size_frame\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\t## Symbol table\n    34\t\n    35\t| # | C symbol (`nm -D`) | type | exported by Rust `.so`? | Rust item |\n    36\t|---|--------------------|------|-------------------------|-----------|\n    37\t| 1 | `max_size_frame`   | `T` (global text) | YES — exact name match | `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn max_size_frame` in `src/lib.rs` |\n    38\t\n    39\t**Missing symbols: 0.** No `#[no_mangle]` wrapper had to be added and no C\n    40\tsource file was left untranslated.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Completeness audit of the C source\n    43\t\n    44\tThe entire C library is two files, reproduced in full so the audit is verifiable:\n    45\t\n    46\t* `c_src/include/lib.h` (5 lines) — `#include <stdint.h>`, one typedef\n    47\t  (`typedef uint32_t tflac_u32;`) and one function declaration. A `typedef`\n    48\t  emits no symbol, so the header contributes exactly one symbol.\n    49\t* `c_src/src/lib.c` (10 lines) — the single definition of `max_size_frame`.\n    50\t  There are no `static` helpers, no additional translation units, no global\n    51\t  variables, and no macro-generated symbol families (verified: `grep -nE\n    52\t  '[*]